.TH KRYX\-SRC 8 "November 2026" "kryx-linux" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
kryx\-src \- unified CRUX/KryX source build, linting, and release\-staging machine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kryx\-src
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ args ...\& ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kryx\-src
is a standalone static Go source\-building and release\-staging companion to
.BR kpm (8),
inspired by Void Linux's
.BR xbps\-src .
It shares
.BR kpm 's
internal Pkgfile parser, builder, package database, and repository indexer while
adding a canonical port registry that resolves ports uniformly by directory path,
basename, declared
.B Pkgfile
.BR name= ,
or collection prefix, across both multi\-collection trees and single\-port repositories.
.SH PORTS DIRECTORY RESOLUTION
.B kryx\-src
never hardcodes or blindly requires
.I /usr/ports
(making it safe for containerized/Docker CI builds).
The ports tree path is resolved in strict priority order:
.IP 1. 4
Explicit CLI flag:
.B \-\-ports\-dir \fIpath\fR
(or
.BR \-P " \fIpath\fR,"
or
.BR \-\-ports " \fIpath\fR)"
.IP 2. 4
Environment variable:
.B $KRYX_PORTS_DIR
or
.B $KPM_PORTS_DIR
.IP 3. 4
Active configuration file
.RB ( [paths] " ports_dir"
in
.IR kpm.ini )
when the directory exists on disk
.IP 4. 4
Workspace auto\-detection in the current working directory:
.IR ./Pkgfile ,
.IR ./.kryx/Pkgfile ,
.IR ./ports ,
or collection directories
.RI ( ./core ,
.IR ./opt ,
.IR ./xorg ,
.IR ./contrib ,
.IR ./compat\-32 ,
.IR ./pkg\-tools ,
.IR ./kernel ,
.IR ./system )
.IP 5. 4
Fallback to
.I /usr/ports
only if the directory exists on disk; otherwise
.B kryx\-src
exits with an actionable error.
.PP
The resolved path is exported as
.B KRYX_PORTS_DIR
and
.B KPM_PORTS_DIR
to child build processes.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B pkg \fR[\fIoptions\fR] \fItarget\fR ... \fR(alias: \fBbuild\fR)
Expand
.I target
arguments (port path, basename, package name, collection name, or
.BR all ),
optionally resolve recursive runtime and make dependencies in topological order
.RB ( \-\-deps ),
satisfy uninstalled dependencies binary\-first from
.I index.json
(or from source with
.BR \-\-source\-deps ),
and compile target archives into
.IR \-\-out\-dir .
.TP
.B plan \fR[\fB\-\-ports\-dir \fIdir\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-ports \fIn\fR] [\fB\-\-chunk\-size \fIn\fR] [\fB\-\-compact\fR] \fItarget\fR ...
Generate a bounded topological GitHub Actions matrix JSON plan.
.TP
.B lint \fR[\fB\-\-ports\-dir \fIdir\fR] [\fB\-\-strict\fR] [\fItarget\fR ...] \fR(alias: \fBcheck\fR)
Validate
.B Pkgfile
recipes across a ports tree, detecting missing required fields, directory\-vs\-name
mismatches, duplicate package names within a collection, missing dependency targets,
and dependency cycles.
.TP
.B list \fR[\fB\-\-ports\-dir \fIdir\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fItarget\fR ...] \fR(alias: \fBls\fR)
List discovered ports with their relative directory path, package name (when it
differs from the directory basename), and full version.
.TP
.B stage \fR[\fIoptions\fR] \fR(alias: \fBindex\fR)
Scan
.I \-\-packages
for CRUX
.I .pkg.tar.<ext>
archives, enrich metadata from
.IR \-\-ports\-dir ,
merge into
.IR \-\-index ,
and optionally copy archives into
.I \-\-upload\-dir
with GitHub\-Releases\-safe filenames
.RB ( #
replaced by
.BR . ).
.TP
.B sign \-\-key \fIprivkey\fR \fR[\fB\-\-signify\fR] [\fB\-\-file \fIindex.json\fR] [\fB\-\-out \fIindex.json.sig\fR]
Generate a detached Ed25519 or OpenBSD
.BR signify (1)\-compatible
signature for
.IR index.json .
.TP
.B rewrite\-urls \-\-index \fIpath\fR \-\-assets\-json \fIfile\fR \fR[\fB\-\-packages \fIdir\fR]
Update download URLs in
.I index.json
using the JSON payload returned by
.B gh release view \-\-json assets
and verify that every built archive resolves to an uploaded asset URL.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.PP
.nf
kryx\-src lint \-\-ports\-dir /workspace/ports
kryx\-src plan \-\-ports\-dir /workspace/ports \-\-compact pkg\-tools/kpm system/dinit
kryx\-src pkg \-\-ports\-dir ./ports \-\-work\-root /tmp/work \-\-out\-dir ./dist/packages \-\-deps \-\-force linux\-6.18
kryx\-src stage \-\-packages ./dist/packages \-\-ports\-dir ./ports \-\-index ./stage/index.json \-\-upload\-dir ./stage/upload
kryx\-src sign \-\-signify \-\-key ./release.sec \-\-file ./stage/index.json
kryx\-src rewrite\-urls \-\-index ./stage/index.json \-\-assets\-json ./stage/assets.json \-\-packages ./dist/packages
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kpm (8),
.BR kpm\-index (8),
.BR gports (8)
